---
# Copy this file to .claude/cc-opencode-cmux.local.md (project root) and adjust.
# The plugin reads these values when starting the serve daemon and dispatching tasks.

# Port for `opencode serve`. Default 4096.
port: 4096

# Hostname. Stay on loopback unless you know what you are doing.
host: 127.0.0.1

# Auto-start the serve daemon on SessionStart.
# Saves the 1.5–2s health-check wait per delegation. Costs one idle daemon.
auto_start: false

# Default model overrides per task type (optional).
# Leave commented to use config/opencode.json.template defaults.
# models:
#   implement: opencode-go/deepseek-v4-pro
#   refactor:  opencode-go/qwen3.6-plus
#   summarize: opencode/gemini-3-flash
#   cjk-doc:   opencode/gemini-3-flash
---

# cc-opencode-cmux local settings

This file is git-ignored. Use it for per-machine overrides like a different daemon port
or a personal preference for which model handles `implement` tasks.

## Authentication

OC Zen and OC Go are **two separate OpenCode subscriptions**. Subscribing to one does
not unlock the other. Both end up authenticated under the same env var
(`OPENCODE_API_KEY`) — `opencode auth login` runs through a TUI menu where you choose
which subscription to authenticate.

### OpenCode Go ($10/month flat, 14 models)

```bash
opencode auth login           # menu: choose "OpenCode Go"
# Browser opens at opencode.ai/auth → subscribe → copy API key → paste back into TUI
```

Models reachable via `opencode-go/<id>`:
- DeepSeek V4 Flash (31,650 req/5h, ctx 1M, biggest quota)
- Qwen 3.5 Plus (10,200 req/5h, ctx 256K)
- DeepSeek V4 Pro (3,450 req/5h, ctx 1M)
- MiniMax M2.7 (3,400 req/5h, ctx 200K)
- Qwen 3.6 Plus (3,300 req/5h, ctx 256K) — best Korean of the Go bunch
- MiMo-V2.5-Pro (1,290 req/5h, ctx 1M)
- Kimi K2.6 (1,150 req/5h, ctx 256K) — SWE-Bench Pro leader
- GLM-5.1 (880 req/5h, ctx 198K)
- (and 6 more: kimi-k2.5, glm-5, minimax-m2.5, mimo-v2.5, mimo-v2-pro, mimo-v2-omni)

### OpenCode Zen (pay-per-token, premium models)

```bash
opencode auth login           # menu: choose "OpenCode Zen"
# Same browser flow → pay-as-you-go (default $20 auto-reload)
```

Models reachable via `opencode/<id>`:
- `opencode/gemini-3-flash`, `opencode/gemini-3.1-pro`
- `opencode/claude-sonnet-4-5`, `opencode/claude-haiku-4-5`
- `opencode/gpt-5.1`, `opencode/gpt-5.4-mini`
- (and ~50 more, see `opencode auth list` after login)

### BYOK (optional fallback, not used automatically)

These bypass the OC gateway. Set whichever you have:

- `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` — any `openrouter/...` model
- `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_API_KEY` — direct provider routes

> **Note**: OpenCode does not support a `fallback_models` config field. The plugin's
> `config/opencode.json.template` lists alternative model IDs in each agent's `description`
> for **manual** fallback — pass the alternative ID to `safe-oc.sh` as the 4th argument
> when the primary model is rate-limited or fails.

## Verifying auth

```bash
opencode auth list
```

If you see at least one provider listed (e.g. `opencode-go`, `opencode`, or a BYOK
provider), authentication is in place.
